{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>For whoever finds me finds life</b> — It includes physical life, why do I need 'life' [meaning] health, the life of the flesh, what does the poor man know to walk against life and sustenance, and 'life for your young women,' and the life of the soul — 'See, I have set before you today life and good,' and the meaning of 'finds me' is 'attains life,' and the sense is 'because he entered peacefully through the way of the openings.'" "<b>And obtains favor from YHWH</b> — He attained favor from his Creator."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:37.068201047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}